&lt;p&gt;Casa del Telaio&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="garden-description"&gt;Garden Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;548.V.4/3.
There was a courtyard (a) in the center of this house which was apparently attached to a &lt;em&gt;textrina&lt;/em&gt;. The courtyard was surrounded by a &lt;em&gt;portico&lt;/em&gt; with seven supporting brick columns. These were connected by a low wall and a second wall on the inside was slightly lower and formed a gutter. A terra-cotta &lt;em&gt;puteal&lt;/em&gt; was located by the entrance on the north over the cistern opening. Maiuri concluded there was enough soil present here to indicate this had been a garden.&lt;/p&gt;
